# Confirmations and dialogs

Never use native browser dialogs (`window.confirm`, `window.alert`, `window.prompt`) for user-facing confirmations or messages. They look out of place next to the QuoteGen UI.

Use an in-app modal instead:
- Overlay: dimmed backdrop (`rgba(15,23,42,.42)`), centered white card, ~20px radius, soft shadow
- Match existing patterns (`WsConvertModal`, Users admin controls): blue `#1A73E8`, slate text, rounded buttons
- Destructive actions: clear title + short consequence text; primary Cancel; danger action styled for hover/confirm
- Escape / backdrop click should cancel when the action is not in progress

Apply this to every new confirm/delete/remove/overwrite flow without waiting for the user to ask.
